<section class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__title">What?</h2>
  <p>
    A swarm of snake robots spell out an input string, powered by reinforcement learning.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <h2 class="content-section__title">How?</h2>

  <p>
    A state-based RL policy controls each snake robot individually. The policy is trained to match a randomly selected pose defined by six target keypoints. The observation space consists of the current state and the target keypoint locations.
  </p>
  <figure class="viz viz--video">
    {{ v.clip("static/videos/training.mp4") }}
  </figure>

  <p>
    To generate target keypoints for a letter, a least squares optimization problem is solved. Given a set of robots spawned evenly along a letter, the solver finds the base locations and joint angles that best cover the letter,
    \[
    \begin{aligned}
    \min_{Q} \;\; & \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} d\big(p_i, V(Q)\big)^2 \;+\; \frac{\lambda}{M} \sum_{j=1}^{M}  d\big(v_j, P\big)^2 \\
    \text{s.t.} \;\; & |\theta_{k,i}| \le \theta_{\max} \; \forall \; k, i
    \end{aligned}
    \]
    where,
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>\(Q = (q_1, \dots, q_K)\) is the configuration of all \(K\) robots with \(q_k = (x_k, y_k, \varphi_k, \theta_{k,1}, \dots, \theta_{k,n-2})\)</li>
    <li>\(P = \{p_1, \dots, p_N\}\) is the set of sampled points on the letter</li>
    <li>\(V(Q) = \{v_1, \dots, v_M\}\) is the set of all vertices of robots in configuration \(Q\)</li>
    <li>\(d(x, S) = \min_{s \in S} \lVert x - s \rVert\) is the distance from a point \(x\) to the nearest point in a set \(S\)</li>
  </ul>

